1
00:00:43,190 --> 00:00:45,790
The next wave of AI is here.
下一波人工智能浪潮已经到来。

2
00:00:46,470 --> 00:00:48,970
Evolving beyond thinking to acting.
从思考进化到行动。

3
00:00:49,530 --> 00:00:51,190
And it's bigger than anyone imagined.
它的规模远超任何人的想象。

4
00:00:51,790 --> 00:00:52,910
Except AMD.
除了 AMD。

5
00:00:54,130 --> 00:01:00,070
We recognize this agentic era would require the highest performing GPUs and CPUs working together.
我们意识到，这一代理时代需要性能最高的 GPU 和 CPU 协同工作。

6
00:01:00,670 --> 00:01:02,650
So we're the only ones who build both.
所以我们是唯一一家同时自研这两者的公司。

7
00:01:03,310 --> 00:01:06,230
It's how agentic AI moves from answers to action.
这正是代理型人工智能从给出答案到付诸行动的关键。

8
00:01:06,550 --> 00:01:09,190
Pushing inference compute to tremendous scale.
将推理计算推向前所未有的规模。

9
00:01:09,990 --> 00:01:16,070
Like an agent that frees thousands of employees from smaller tasks to focus on bigger things.
就像一个代理，让成千上万的员工从琐碎任务中解放出来，专注于更重要的事情。

10
00:01:17,210 --> 00:01:22,050
A car that safely handles a new city like a local on its first day there.
一辆汽车，能在第一天就如本地人般安全地应对陌生城市。

11
00:01:24,490 --> 00:01:30,710
And an agent that pinpoints a disease in millions of cells, then designs a cure.
还有一个代理，能在数百万个细胞中精准定位疾病，然后设计出疗法。

12
00:01:33,130 --> 00:01:39,290
We've built more AI computing power into a single data center than existed on Earth a decade ago.
我们在一个数据中心内构建的 AI 计算能力，超过了十年前地球上所有计算能力的总和。

13
00:01:40,470 --> 00:01:43,190
And now, we're giving you the tools.
现在，我们为您提供工具。

14
00:01:45,030 --> 00:01:47,490
So together, we advance AI.
让我们一起推动人工智能的发展。

15
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:08,120
Good morning!
早上好！

16
00:02:09,940 --> 00:02:11,780
That's a pretty good good morning.
这真是个不错的早上。

17
00:02:12,460 --> 00:02:13,820
Good morning!
早上好！

18
00:02:13,820 --> 00:02:15,240
Good morning!
早上好！

19
00:02:15,940 --> 00:02:18,800
And welcome to Advancing AI 2026.
欢迎参加“推动人工智能 2026”大会。

20
00:02:19,200 --> 00:02:24,800
It's so great to be back here in San Francisco and to see so many friends and partners and customers.
很高兴再次回到旧金山，见到这么多朋友、合作伙伴和客户。

21
00:02:25,340 --> 00:02:28,740
And especially all the developers that are here with us today.
尤其欢迎今天在场的所有开发者。

22
00:02:29,340 --> 00:02:33,660
And I want to say a big welcome to everyone who's joining us online from around the world.
我要向全球各地在线加入我们的所有人表示热烈欢迎。

23
00:02:34,620 --> 00:02:37,980
This is my absolute favorite event of the year.
这是我一年中最喜欢的活动。

24
00:02:38,180 --> 00:02:43,280
It's where we bring the entire AI ecosystem together to show what we've been building.
这里汇聚了整个 AI 生态系统，展示我们所打造的一切。

25
00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:44,680
And where we're going next.
以及我们接下来要去的地方。

26
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:47,540
And this year, this is our biggest show ever.
今年，这是我们规模最大的一次展会。

27
00:02:47,720 --> 00:02:49,800
Because we have so much to tell you.
因为我们有太多内容要告诉你们。

28
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:51,720
So let's go ahead and get started.
那么，让我们开始吧。

29
00:02:53,720 --> 00:03:01,240
At AMD, our mission is to push the boundaries of high performance in AI computing to help solve the world's most important challenges.
在 AMD，我们的使命是推动人工智能计算高性能的边界，以帮助解决世界上最紧迫的挑战。

30
00:03:02,100 --> 00:03:07,220
And I often say, AI is the most important technology of the last 50 years.
我经常说，人工智能是过去50年里最重要的技术。

31
00:03:08,040 --> 00:03:12,180
And frankly, the progress that we're seeing in the industry is just incredible.
说实话，我们看到的行业进展简直令人惊叹。

32
00:03:12,180 --> 00:03:18,060
Like, every month, every few months, we see something new that was far beyond our imagination.
每个月，甚至每过几个月，我们都会看到一些远超我们想象的新突破。

33
00:03:18,820 --> 00:03:22,080
And you can already see the impact across every industry.
你已经可以看到它对每个行业产生的影响。

34
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:27,620
In healthcare, AI is helping researchers identify new drug candidates faster.
在医疗健康领域，人工智能正在帮助研究人员更快地发现新的药物候选。

35
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:32,980
In science, we're solving problems that we didn't think were possible a few years ago.
在科学领域，我们正在解决几年前还觉得不可能的问题。

36
00:03:33,520 --> 00:03:37,780
And across every industry, AI is changing the way we get work done.
在每个行业，人工智能正在改变我们完成工作的模式。

37
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:44,940
And the most important thing is we're still in the very, very early innings of what's possible.
最重要的是，我们仍处于可能性的非常非常早期阶段。

38
00:03:46,300 --> 00:03:48,300
Now, just take a look at some of these charts.
现在，请看一下这些图表。

39
00:03:48,460 --> 00:03:49,880
You know, we look at these every year.
我们每年都看这些数据。

40
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:53,940
And you kind of see the rate and pace of AI growth.
你就能看出人工智能增长的速度和节奏。

41
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:56,720
A couple of years ago, we were just starting.
几年前，我们才刚刚起步。

42
00:03:57,060 --> 00:03:58,960
People were experimenting with chatbots.
人们还在尝试聊天机器人。

43
00:03:59,320 --> 00:04:00,640
And, you know, it was really cool.
那时候真的很酷。

44
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:08,280
But if you look at today, we're really seeing more than 35 quadrillion tokens consumed every single month.
但如果你看看今天，我们每月消耗的词元已超过35千万亿。

45
00:04:09,360 --> 00:04:13,480
That's an increase of nearly 160 times in just two years.
这仅仅两年间就增长了近160倍。

46
00:04:14,200 --> 00:04:17,100
And that curve is actually just getting steeper.
而且这条曲线实际上正在变得越来越陡。

47
00:04:17,140 --> 00:04:18,620
You're going to hear a lot about that today.
今天你们会听到很多关于这一点的内容。

48
00:04:19,840 --> 00:04:22,580
So, just looking at, you know, where is all that demand?
所以，简单来说，这些需求到底来自哪里？

49
00:04:22,780 --> 00:04:26,320
I mean, obviously, training remains incredibly important and foundational.
我的意思是，显然，训练仍然极其重要且是基础性的。

50
00:04:26,320 --> 00:04:36,060
And over the last four or five years, you know, we see the compute that's used for training advanced models continuing to increase by, let's call it, roughly 5x every year.
在过去四五年里，我们看到用于训练先进模型的算力，每年大约增长5倍。

51
00:04:36,720 --> 00:04:38,060
And those models are getting better.
这些模型正在变得越来越好。

52
00:04:38,260 --> 00:04:39,540
Like, we're all experiencing that.
就像我们每个人都在亲身经历这一点。

53
00:04:39,620 --> 00:04:40,540
We're seeing better reasoning.
我们看到了更出色的推理能力。

54
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:42,060
We're seeing new capabilities.
我们看到了新的能力。

55
00:04:42,540 --> 00:04:45,660
We're now seeing a growing number of specialized models.
我们现在正看到越来越多的专用模型。

56
00:04:45,880 --> 00:04:50,500
And one of the things that I really believe in is there is no one perfect model.
我坚信的一点是，不存在一个完美的模型。

57
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:57,760
I think we're all going to use a slew of different models, depending on what task you're trying to solve and which industry you're in.
我认为我们都会根据要解决的任务和所在行业，使用大量不同的模型。

58
00:04:58,800 --> 00:05:01,540
But the bigger shift is actually in inference.
但更大的转变实际上发生在推理阶段。

59
00:05:02,240 --> 00:05:03,360
And we expected this.
我们早就预料到了这一点。

60
00:05:03,480 --> 00:05:06,620
We expected that inference would grow faster than training.
我们早就预料到推理的增长速度会超过训练。

61
00:05:07,040 --> 00:05:15,200
And we can say that in 2026, for the first time, the world is using more AI compute to run models than to train them.
到2026年，全球用于运行模型的AI算力将首次超过用于训练模型的算力。

62
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:24,140
And we've seen that to a point where we think this year, roughly 60% of the global AI compute capacity will be used for inference.
我们已经看到这一趋势，预计今年全球约60%的AI算力将用于推理。

63
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:27,740
And the reason for that is actually pretty simple.
造成这一现象的原因其实相当简单。

64
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:35,420
As billions of people every day use AI, the workload shifts from building models to putting them to work.
随着数十亿人每天使用AI，工作负载正从构建模型转向让模型投入实际应用。

65
00:05:36,020 --> 00:05:42,380
And actually, we're going to talk a lot today about agentic AI, and that's accelerating the shift even faster.
事实上，今天我们将会大量讨论代理型AI，这正在加速这一转变。

66
00:05:42,380 --> 00:05:49,040
So if you think about all of this, we see agents as the next big step for AI.
因此，如果我们思考这一切，我们认为代理是AI发展的下一步重大飞跃。

67
00:05:49,760 --> 00:05:57,180
And the most interesting thing is this has really just started accelerating over the last, I would say, five or six months this year.
最有趣的是，这种加速趋势实际上才刚刚开始，大概从今年五到六个月前才真正显现。

68
00:05:57,960 --> 00:06:01,340
So when we started with LLMs, they were great to answer questions.
当我们最初开发大语言模型时，它们主要用于回答问题。

69
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:10,100
But we found that to really get the power of AI, you want agents to be able to really answer full questions.
但后来我们发现，要真正发挥AI的潜力，需要让代理能够完整地回答复杂问题。

70
00:06:10,100 --> 00:06:14,420
So you give it a goal, it keeps working until it's solved the problem.
你只需设定一个目标，它就会持续工作，直到问题被解决。

71
00:06:15,420 --> 00:06:23,460
And what that means for us in the compute industry, it means that compute demand is growing at an incredible pace.
这对算力行业意味着，算力需求正以惊人的速度增长。

72
00:06:23,860 --> 00:06:27,120
We're actually seeing a step change in compute demand.
我们实际上正在见证算力需求的一次质的飞跃。

73
00:06:27,840 --> 00:06:33,120
Because when you ask the agent to do something, it actually has dozens of steps.
因为当你让代理执行某项任务时，它实际上需要完成数十个步骤。

74
00:06:33,260 --> 00:06:37,100
And it has to reason, and it has to call tools, and it has to access data.
它必须进行推理，调用工具，并访问数据。

75
00:06:37,100 --> 00:06:40,380
And it has to keep doing it over and over until it's solved the problem.
它必须反复执行这些操作，直到问题得到解决。

76
00:06:40,980 --> 00:06:43,720
And so you need lots of GPUs to do all that reasoning.
因此你需要大量GPU来完成所有这些推理任务。

77
00:06:44,600 --> 00:06:49,780
But importantly, you also need a lot of CPUs to orchestrate every step around it.
但更重要的是，你还需要大量CPU来协调每一个步骤。

78
00:06:50,960 --> 00:06:57,600
So when you look at just what that means from a market standpoint, it's really hard to put this market data up.
所以当你从市场角度看待这一点时，很难将这些市场数据呈现出来。

79
00:06:57,800 --> 00:07:03,000
Because I feel like every few months, we're changing the perspective based on what our customers are saying.
因为我觉得每隔几个月，我们都会根据客户反馈改变视角。

80
00:07:03,880 --> 00:07:11,780
But what we're seeing is that the shift to agentic AI is certainly growing the AI accelerator market very significantly.
但我们看到的是，向代理式AI的转变确实显著推动了AI加速器市场的增长。

81
00:07:13,120 --> 00:07:20,440
It was actually last year at this event that we called the AI accelerator market at about 500 billion by 2028.
其实去年在本次活动中，我们就预测AI加速器市场将在2028年达到约5000亿。

82
00:07:21,060 --> 00:07:24,640
And at that time, it actually felt like a very big number.
当时这个数字看起来非常庞大。

83
00:07:26,440 --> 00:07:27,460
Didn't you think it was a big number?
你不觉得这个数字很大吗？

84
00:07:29,060 --> 00:07:31,800
But honestly, you look at it today, and it looks conservative.
但说实话，现在再看，这个预测显得有些保守了。

85
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:35,780
Because the AI demand is just continuing to accelerate.
因为AI需求仍在持续加速。

86
00:07:36,460 --> 00:07:37,300
And you can see it, right?
你能看出来，对吧？

87
00:07:37,420 --> 00:07:41,180
Better models, more usage, more usage requires more compute.
更好的模型，更多的使用，更多的使用需要更多的算力。

88
00:07:41,620 --> 00:07:44,300
And more compute actually builds better models.
更多的计算能力实际上能构建出更好的模型。

89
00:07:44,780 --> 00:07:53,260
And so we're now expecting that by 2030, the AI accelerator market is going to reach about 1.4 trillion by 2030.
因此我们预计到2030年，AI加速器市场规模将达到约1.4万亿美元。

90
00:07:53,820 --> 00:07:54,820
So what do you think about that?
你觉得怎么样？

91
00:07:54,820 --> 00:07:55,580
Is that a big number?
那是很大的数字吗？

92
00:08:00,380 --> 00:08:09,540
I mean, what that means is by the end of the decade, the AI accelerator market is going to approach the size of the entire semiconductor market today.
我的意思是，到本十年末，AI加速器市场的规模将接近当今整个半导体市场的规模。

93
00:08:10,600 --> 00:08:17,820
And although there will be many different types of accelerators, you know, I'm a big believer in there's no one size fits all as it comes to chips.
尽管会有各种不同类型的加速器，但我始终相信，芯片并不存在一种放之四海而皆准的通用方案。

94
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:27,820
We do expect that GPUs are going to make up the vast majority of that market because the algorithms are still very much in their infancy, and we're still
我们预计GPU将占据该市场绝大部分，因为相关算法仍处于非常初期的阶段，我们仍在

95
00:08:27,820 --> 00:08:35,640
continuing to see the workloads change, and that favors programmability in the overall silicon ecosystem.
持续看到工作负载的变化，这有利于整个硅基生态系统的可编程性。

96
00:08:37,020 --> 00:08:44,120
Now, perhaps the most interesting part of the last six months has been, you know, GPUs are only part of this story.
现在，过去六个月里最有趣的部分或许是，你知道的，GPU 只是这个故事的一部分。

97
00:08:45,160 --> 00:08:51,440
What we're actually seeing is agentic AI is creating an entirely new growth vector for server CPUs.
我们实际上看到的是，代理型AI正在为服务器CPU创造一个全新的增长方向。

98
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:57,900
Now, I've updated this number a lot also over the last, you know, six to eight months.
近六到八个月来，我也多次更新过这个数字。

99
00:08:58,380 --> 00:09:02,360
But look, we call it like we see it, and we were early.
但我们要说的是我们看到的实际情况，而且我们很早就意识到了这一点。

100
00:09:02,640 --> 00:09:12,480
I mean, we saw from our largest hyperscale customers, and you're going to see some of them here today, who said, look, as AI inference is going up, we need more server CPUs.
我们从最大的超大规模客户那里就看到了这一点，你们今天也会看到其中一些客户，他们说：随着AI推理需求上升，我们需要更多的服务器CPU。

101
00:09:12,720 --> 00:09:17,580
And so we saw growth in the server CPU market, and we said, you know,
于是我们看到了服务器CPU市场的增长，于是我们说，

102
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:24,060
last year we thought it might grow, let's call it 18 to 20% CAGR, to an overall market size of 60 billion.
去年我们预计它可能以18%到20%的年复合增长率增长，市场规模达到600亿。

103
00:09:24,760 --> 00:09:31,560
But frankly, what we're seeing is that the rate and pace of agentic AI adoption is much, much faster than any of us thought.
但坦率地说，我们看到的是，代理型AI的采用速度远比我们任何人预想的要快得多。

104
00:09:32,620 --> 00:09:44,020
So we're talking about agents going from millions to billions, like we're able to increase all of our productivity, and that requires a tremendous amount of CPU infrastructure.
所以我们现在看到的是，代理从数百万增长到数十亿，我们能够大幅提升所有生产力，而这需要庞大的CPU基础设施。

105
00:09:44,020 --> 00:09:49,180
And every customer conversation is telling us that this build-out is just beginning.
每一次客户对话都在告诉我们，这场基础设施建设才刚刚开始。

106
00:09:50,140 --> 00:09:59,060
So based on what we're seeing today, and we're going to talk more about how agentic AI is evolving with CPUs, we now expect the server CPU market to
因此，基于我们今天所看到的情况，我们接下来会更多讨论代理型AI如何与CPU共同演进，我们现在预计服务器CPU市场将

107
00:09:59,060 --> 00:10:03,920
grow by over 50% to over 200 billion by 2030.
到2030年增长超过50%，达到2000亿以上。

108
00:10:04,600 --> 00:10:10,040
So that's starting from today, a $25 billion market going to over 200 billion.
也就是说，从现在的250亿市场，增长到超过2000亿。

109
00:10:10,040 --> 00:10:14,280
So there's a lot of excitement about CPUs as well.
因此，人们对CPU也充满期待。

110
00:10:16,020 --> 00:10:25,460
Now, probably one of the things that is differentiating AMD in how we think about the market is this is not just a data center opportunity.
现在，可能有一件事让AMD在看待市场时与其他公司不同，那就是这不仅仅是一个数据中心的机会。

111
00:10:26,180 --> 00:10:34,340
As AI becomes a larger part of our daily lives, we want the intelligence to run right where the work happens.
随着人工智能在我们日常生活中扮演越来越重要的角色，我们希望智能计算能就在工作发生的地方运行。

112
00:10:34,820 --> 00:10:40,900
And that means cloud is super important, but the devices that we use every day are going to be extremely important.
这意味着云至关重要，但我们每天使用的设备也将变得极为重要。

113
00:10:41,440 --> 00:10:48,100
And that means that we're going to do a lot more at the edge as well with autonomous machines that sense and act in real time.
这意味着我们还需要在边缘侧做更多事情，比如让能够实时感知和行动的自主机器发挥作用。

114
00:10:48,880 --> 00:10:52,360
And we really believe that you need AI to be infused everywhere.
我们真正相信，人工智能必须无处不在。

115
00:10:52,920 --> 00:10:55,200
And that's exactly what we're focused on at AMD.
这正是AMD专注的方向。

116
00:10:56,320 --> 00:11:04,940
So putting all of that together, we actually expect that the market for our high-performance and adaptive computing products to grow at roughly a 40% CAGR
因此，综合来看，我们预计高性能和自适应计算产品市场在未来几年将以约40%的年复合增长率扩张。

117
00:11:04,940 --> 00:11:09,980
over the next several years, approaching a $2 trillion market by 2030.
到2030年，市场规模将接近2万亿美元。

118
00:11:11,140 --> 00:11:17,740
And frankly, the only way you're going to be able to service a market like that is for us to work together as an ecosystem.
诚实地讲，要服务这样一个市场，唯一的办法就是我们作为生态系统共同协作。

119
00:11:18,320 --> 00:11:25,300
There's no one company that can solve it all, but this is the opportunity to bring the best and brightest together.
没有任何一家公司能独自解决所有问题，但这也是汇聚最优秀人才的绝佳机会。

