谢谢你，萨钦。

409
00:38:57,220 --> 00:38:57,900
Thank you so much.
非常感谢。

410
00:38:58,120 --> 00:39:04,870
Yes. Alright.
好的。

411
00:39:05,090 --> 00:39:07,810
So now let's turn to the world of CPUs.
那么现在我们转向 CPU 的世界。

412
00:39:08,990 --> 00:39:17,010
There's been a lot of talk about CPUs recently, and I can say that this has been the foundation of our AMD data center strategy for the longest time.
近期关于 CPU 的讨论非常多，我可以告诉大家，这一直是 AMD 数据中心战略的基石，时间最长。

413
00:39:17,670 --> 00:39:22,550
We launched EPYC in 2017, and we've been on a very, very clear mission.
我们在 2017 年推出了 EPYC，一直有着非常明确的目标。

414
00:39:23,230 --> 00:39:30,970
Every generation, more performance, more efficiency, more capability for a wider range of workloads.
每一代都带来更高的性能、更高的效率、更强的能力，支持更广泛的工作负载。

415
00:39:31,450 --> 00:39:32,990
Now, Naples was our first generation.
现在，Naples 是我们的第一代产品。

416
00:39:33,410 --> 00:39:38,550
It established the foundation, but Rome and Milan really changed the economics in the data center.
它奠定了基础，但 Rome 和 Milan 才真正改变了数据中心的经济格局。

417
00:39:38,770 --> 00:39:44,190
We did more than what people expected in terms of adding core count and adding throughput.
我们在核心数量和吞吐量方面所实现的，远超人们的预期。

418
00:39:44,910 --> 00:39:53,010
And then Turin set... Genoa expanded our performance, and then Turin set a new bar for density, throughput, and total cost of ownership.
然后 Turin 推出了……Genoa 进一步提升了性能，而 Turin 则在密度、吞吐量和总拥有成本方面树立了新标准。

419
00:39:53,630 --> 00:39:55,550
That's really been the EPYC formula.
这正是 EPYC 的成功公式。

420
00:39:55,550 --> 00:40:03,370
A clear roadmap and very consistent execution, and leadership that actually grows with every generation.
清晰的路线图和一贯的执行，以及每一代都在持续提升的领导力。

421
00:40:04,330 --> 00:40:09,510
This is why, if you look today, 5th Gen EPYC Turin is the best server CPU in the world.
这就是为什么，如果你今天查看，第五代 EPYC Turin 是全球最佳的服务器 CPU。

422
00:40:10,290 --> 00:40:21,530
With up to 192 cores and 384 threads, Turin delivers leadership performance across a broad range of cloud, enterprise, and HPC workloads.
Turin 最多可提供 192 个核心和 384 个线程，在云、企业及高性能计算等多种工作负载中均表现出领先性能。

423
00:40:21,810 --> 00:40:25,790
But the thing about the data center is compute never stands still.
但数据中心的计算能力从来不会停滞不前。

424
00:40:26,950 --> 00:40:34,110
With agentic AI, it's actually creating a whole new class of infrastructure, and the CPU matters now more than ever.
有了代理式 AI，实际上正在催生一类全新的基础设施，而 CPU 的重要性如今比以往任何时候都更大。

425
00:40:34,790 --> 00:40:37,650
And that's exactly what we built Venice for.
这正是我们打造 Venice 的原因。

426
00:40:38,630 --> 00:40:42,930
So, there's been a lot of talk about agentic AI, but it's actually a very new field.
因此，关于代理式 AI 的讨论很多，但事实上这是一个非常新的领域。

427
00:40:43,310 --> 00:40:49,890
And what we see is that server computing is actually splitting across a couple of different workloads.
我们看到的是，服务器计算实际上正在向几类不同的工作负载分化。

428
00:40:49,890 --> 00:40:55,470
So, the first section is GPU servers, and that's fairly well known.
第一个部分是 GPU 服务器，这一点大家已经很熟悉。

429
00:40:56,090 --> 00:41:00,650
That's where the CPU's job is basically to drive the GPUs.
在这里，CPU 的主要任务就是驱动 GPU。

430
00:41:01,230 --> 00:41:04,370
And so, the job there is all about speed.
因此，这里的重点完全在于速度。

431
00:41:05,030 --> 00:41:10,570
We want the highest frequency cores, we want the fastest IO, and we want to keep the GPUs fully fed.
我们需要最高频率的核心，最快的 I/O，还要确保 GPU 始终得到充分供给。

432
00:41:11,850 --> 00:41:18,030
Now, the biggest middle part, this is the largest growth, is actually in agent servers, or what we call agent sandboxes.
现在，最大的中间部分，也就是增长最快的领域，实际上是代理服务器，或我们所说的代理沙盒。

433
00:41:18,790 --> 00:41:21,570
And this is actually a whole new class of workload.
而这实际上是一个全新的工作负载类别。

434
00:41:22,010 --> 00:41:31,370
Here, you execute code, you actually call a bunch of tools, you actually query data that's outside the model, you have a whole bunch of things around it.
在这里，你执行代码，实际调用大量工具，实际查询模型外部的数据，周围还有一系列其他功能。

435
00:41:31,650 --> 00:41:35,110
And in this place, the priority is actually density.
在这个领域，优先考虑的是密度。

436
00:41:35,390 --> 00:41:42,050
So, we want the highest performing cores per watt to run thousands of agents at once.
因此，我们希望每瓦特功耗下拥有最高性能的核心，以同时运行数千个代理。

437
00:41:42,770 --> 00:41:47,090
And then we have our traditional general purpose servers that run the enterprise.
然后我们还有传统的通用服务器，用于运行企业级应用。

438
00:41:47,090 --> 00:41:50,150
And here, you're going to have a diversity of workloads.
在这里，你将面对多样化的工作负载。

439
00:41:50,150 --> 00:41:55,090
It's all about efficiency, it's running the applications, it's running databases, it's running data services.
这一切关乎效率，是运行应用程序，运行数据库，运行数据服务。

440
00:41:55,730 --> 00:42:01,190
And all of that is what we traditionally say is general purpose server.
所有这些就是我们传统意义上所说的通用服务器。

441
00:42:01,830 --> 00:42:07,310
And so, with these different workloads, you actually need the right CPU for the right workload.
因此，面对这些不同的工作负载，你实际上需要为每种工作负载配备合适的CPU。

442
00:42:07,890 --> 00:42:12,730
And EPYC is the only CPU portfolio that leads across all three.
而EPYC是唯一一个在所有三个领域都领先的CPU产品组合。

443
00:42:13,690 --> 00:42:21,230
So, Venice is our newest and most advanced server CPU family, and it's actually designed for the agentic era.
因此，威尼斯是我们最新、最先进的服务器CPU系列，实际上是为代理时代而设计的。

444
00:42:22,150 --> 00:42:25,690
We're extending Turin's leadership across every single metric.
我们正在将图灵的领先地位扩展到每一个指标上。

445
00:42:25,890 --> 00:42:33,730
That is performance, that's efficiency, that's TCO for cloud, that's enterprise efficiency, that's HPC workloads.
这是性能，这是效率，这是云服务的总拥有成本，这是企业效率，这是高性能计算工作负载。

446
00:42:34,430 --> 00:42:37,190
And Venice starts with our all new Zen 6 core.
代号威尼斯从我们全新的Zen 6核心开始。

447
00:42:38,290 --> 00:42:45,970
We have higher IPC, higher frequency, and that delivers up to 1.8 times more performance than Turin.
我们拥有更高的每时钟周期指令数、更高的频率，性能相比图林最高提升1.8倍。

448
00:42:46,730 --> 00:42:49,730
That is one of the largest generational gains.
这是历史上最大的一代性能提升之一。

449
00:42:49,850 --> 00:42:55,890
I mean, we have been doing this for six generations, but this is one of the largest generational gains in the history of EPYC.
我们已经连续六代这么做，但这是EPYC历史上最大的一代性能提升之一。

450
00:42:56,970 --> 00:43:08,030
It's 203 billion transistors built on TSMC's newest two nanometer process, and it uses a next generation chiplet that supports up to 512 threads per socket.
它拥有2030亿个晶体管，采用台积电最新的2纳米工艺制造，采用新一代小芯片架构，每插槽支持高达512个线程。

451
00:43:08,330 --> 00:43:10,390
And this is actually a really important point.
这实际上是一个非常关键的点。

452
00:43:10,390 --> 00:43:12,350
I'm going to show you why in a few minutes.
我稍后会向你们展示原因。

453
00:43:13,370 --> 00:43:19,590
This gives us the highest compute density, but it also allows us to double both the memory and the IO bandwidth.
这使我们实现了最高的计算密度，同时也让内存和I/O带宽翻倍。

454
00:43:20,290 --> 00:43:24,010
So I have a few more chips to show you, if that's all right.
如果可以的话，我再向大家展示几款芯片。

455
00:43:25,290 --> 00:43:29,470
And what's clear is Venice is not one chip.
显而易见，威尼斯并非单一芯片。

456
00:43:30,430 --> 00:43:33,330
Venice is actually an entire family of chips.
威尼斯实际上是一整套芯片家族。

457
00:43:33,910 --> 00:43:38,310
And this is where our chiplet architecture becomes a huge, huge advantage.
这正是我们的芯片小片架构发挥巨大优势的地方。

458
00:43:38,310 --> 00:43:44,270
It lets us take the Zen 6 architecture and build a whole portfolio around it.
它让我们能够基于 Zen 6 架构构建一整套产品组合。

459
00:43:44,830 --> 00:43:46,350
So let's start with this guy.
那么我们先从这个开始。

460
00:43:48,150 --> 00:43:50,010
This is Venice HF.
这是 Venice HF。

461
00:43:51,230 --> 00:43:56,690
This is the highest performing CPU that drives AI host nodes.
这是驱动 AI 主机节点性能最高的 CPU。

462
00:43:57,630 --> 00:44:07,270
It has eight compute chiplets, each with 12 cores, running at up to 5 gigahertz with the IO and memory bandwidth to keep the GPUs completely fed.
它拥有八个计算小片，每个小片配备 12 个核心，最高运行频率达 5 吉赫兹，并具备足够的 I/O 和内存带宽，确保 GPU 充分供能。

463
00:44:07,270 --> 00:44:11,070
And this is the CPU that I showed you before shipping inside Helios.
这就是我之前在 Helios 内部展示过的 CPU。

464
00:44:20,890 --> 00:44:23,530
Now, this is its bigger brother.
现在这是它的升级版。

465
00:44:24,210 --> 00:44:26,310
It's Venice 256 core.
这是拥有 256 个核心的 Venice。

466
00:44:26,930 --> 00:44:30,450
This is the chip that's built for agentic sandboxes.
这颗芯片专为智能体沙盒设计。

467
00:44:30,790 --> 00:44:35,830
And it also has eight compute chiplets, but each of the chiplets now has 32 cores.
它同样拥有八个计算小片，但每个小片现在拥有 32 个核心。

468
00:44:35,970 --> 00:44:39,350
So it scales all the way to 512 threads.
因此它可扩展至 512 个线程。

469
00:44:39,350 --> 00:44:42,910
And it is the highest compute density in the industry.
这是业界最高的计算密度。

470
00:44:49,060 --> 00:44:54,120
Customers get more agent capacity per watt, per dollar, per rack, bar none.
客户在每瓦特、每美元、每机架的算力上都获得了最大提升，毫无例外。

471
00:44:58,270 --> 00:45:00,890
Okay, and then one more member of the family.
好的，接下来再介绍一位家族成员。

472
00:45:01,490 --> 00:45:04,090
This one is Venice 128 core.
这款是威尼斯 128 核。

473
00:45:04,650 --> 00:45:07,990
And this guy is optimized for enterprise and general purpose servers.
这款专为企事业单位和通用服务器优化。

474
00:45:08,510 --> 00:45:15,870
This is the same leadership performance per core, but it's in a lower cost, lower power design for enterprise applications.
每核性能保持领先，但采用了成本更低、功耗更低的设计，适用于企业应用。

475
00:45:16,630 --> 00:45:22,870
And this one is really tuned to give customers the best performance per dollar across a wide range of configurations.
这款产品在各种配置下，为客户实现了每美元性能的最佳表现。

476
00:45:23,010 --> 00:45:27,670
So you can see really the power of the family as they come together.
所以你可以真正看到整个产品家族协同带来的强大优势。

477
00:45:28,370 --> 00:45:33,930
And in addition with these guys, I can tell you that next year we're adding a few other chips to the family.
此外，这些产品之外，明年我们还将为这个家族新增几款芯片。

478
00:45:34,130 --> 00:45:38,170
We're adding Verano, which is the next generation for AI host nodes.
我们将推出 Verano，这是下一代 AI 主机节点。

479
00:45:38,170 --> 00:45:46,170
And what that adds is a more power efficient, low power memory, as well as faster interconnect between the CPU and the GPU.
它带来了更省电、低功耗的内存，以及 CPU 和 GPU 之间更快的互连。

480
00:45:46,750 --> 00:45:55,510
And then we're also adding for our high performance computing, our technical computing, Venice X, which is using our 3D vCache stacking technology.
此外，我们还将为高性能计算和专业技术计算推出威尼斯 X，它采用了我们的 3D vCache 堆叠技术。

481
00:45:55,510 --> 00:46:04,330
And we're really the first to stack memory chiplets right below the compute chiplets to accelerate performance, even for those types of workloads.
我们是首个将内存小芯片直接堆叠在计算小芯片下方的公司，从而加速性能，即使是针对这类工作负载也是如此。

482
00:46:04,330 --> 00:46:06,430
So you can see one architecture.
所以你可以看到一种架构。

483
00:46:06,430 --> 00:46:08,790
A CPU is not a CPU.
CPU 并不都是 CPU。

484
00:46:09,570 --> 00:46:11,090
There are many different types of CPUs.
存在多种不同类型的 CPU。

485
00:46:11,950 --> 00:46:15,630
And for us, one architecture spans dozens of different chips.
对我们而言，一种架构覆盖了数十种不同的芯片。

486
00:46:16,130 --> 00:46:20,130
And that breadth is someone that no other CPU vendor can match.
这种广度是其他任何 CPU 厂商都无法匹敌的。

487
00:46:20,450 --> 00:46:24,950
And that's what makes 6th Gen EPYC the best CPU in the data center.
这正是第六代 EPYC 成为数据中心最佳 CPU 的原因。

488
00:46:31,980 --> 00:46:36,860
Now you're going to bear with me because I'm going to take you through some performance because the numbers are just incredible.
现在请耐心听我说，我将带你们看看一些性能数据，因为这些数字实在太惊人了。

489
00:46:38,000 --> 00:46:40,160
So looking at AI workloads, right?
所以我们来看一下 AI 工作负载。

490
00:46:40,160 --> 00:46:46,280
Again, you have different use cases and different workloads, starting first with GPU servers.
再次强调，存在不同的使用场景和工作负载，首先是 GPU 服务器。

491
00:46:47,020 --> 00:46:52,280
Many of the largest frontier models require you to move data between the CPU and the GPU.
许多最前沿的模型需要在 CPU 和 GPU 之间移动数据。

492
00:46:52,800 --> 00:47:02,680
And in that scenario, Venice moves the data faster than the best competitive x86 processor, delivering up to 1.8 times more tokens per second.
在这种场景下，Venice 的数据传输速度比最佳的竞争对手 x86 处理器更快，每秒可处理多达 1.8 倍的词元。

493
00:47:03,680 --> 00:47:12,160
And when you look at the agentic CPU servers and sandboxes, because of our density, Venice delivers more than twice the agents per watt for agent sandboxes.
当你观察代理型CPU服务器和沙盒时，由于我们的密度优势，威尼斯在代理沙盒中每瓦特的代理数量超过两倍。

494
00:47:13,280 --> 00:47:18,320
And for general purpose applications, in this case, we're standardizing on a 100 kilowatt rack.
对于通用应用，我们在此情况下采用100千瓦机架的标准。

495
00:47:18,880 --> 00:47:22,000
Venice delivers more than twice the performance per watt.
威尼斯每瓦特的性能超过两倍。

496
00:47:22,360 --> 00:47:25,220
So pretty incredible results.
因此结果非常惊人。

497
00:47:26,480 --> 00:47:30,520
And the gap is even wider if you look at ARM processors.
如果你再看ARM处理器，差距会更大。

498
00:47:31,240 --> 00:47:40,060
So if you look at the leading ARM processors, when we're comparing at the chip level, Venice supports up to 2.8 times more agents per watt.
因此，当我们在芯片层面进行比较时，威尼斯每瓦特支持的代理数量最多可达领先ARM处理器的2.8倍。

499
00:47:40,860 --> 00:47:47,020
And when you look at the rack level, Venice is delivering up to 3.3 times more performance per watt.
而在机架层面，威尼斯每瓦特的性能最高可达3.3倍。

500
00:47:47,800 --> 00:47:56,000
And what that means is at the data center scale, you can just get a lot more agents in the same power envelope.
这意味着在数据中心规模上，你可以在相同的功耗范围内部署更多代理。

501
00:48:03,300 --> 00:48:12,580
Now, there's been a lot of talk about what matters most for agentic AI, with some saying that per-core performance under load is the only thing that counts.
近来关于代理型AI最关键的因素有很多讨论，有人认为负载下的每核性能才是唯一重要的。

502
00:48:13,340 --> 00:48:24,420
But that's really only part of the story, because agentic AI actually runs as a distributed platform, and that is across databases and vector stores and orchestration.
但这只是故事的一部分，因为代理型AI实际上是一个分布式平台，涉及数据库、向量存储和编排。

503
00:48:24,900 --> 00:48:27,140
And all of that has to happen at once.
所有这些必须同时发生。

504
00:48:27,480 --> 00:48:37,060
And that requires not just raw speed, but you absolutely need density, efficiency, and per-core performance all together.
这不仅需要原始速度，更需要密度、效率和每核性能三者兼备。

505
00:48:37,060 --> 00:48:42,420
And what I'm happy to say is that Venice leads across every one of them.
我很高兴地告诉大家，威尼斯在所有这些方面都处于领先地位。

506
00:48:43,220 --> 00:48:52,900
So when you compare Venice against the highest performing ARM CPU from our competition, EPYC delivers 20% higher per-core performance.
因此，当您将威尼斯与竞争对手最高效的ARM CPU进行对比时，EPYC的单核性能高出20%。

507
00:48:53,900 --> 00:48:54,400
And when we...
当我们将这一点……

508
00:48:59,690 --> 00:49:01,010
I like that number.
我喜欢这个数字。

509
00:49:01,790 --> 00:49:02,530
I like that number.
我喜欢这个数字。

510
00:49:03,270 --> 00:49:09,450
And when we pair that with leadership core density, we're delivering 2.2 times more performance at the socket level.
再加上领先的核心密度，我们在插槽级别实现了2.2倍的性能提升。

511
00:49:09,450 --> 00:49:17,610
And so the main point is, whether a customer needs per-core or per-socket performance, Venice is the leader.
所以核心要点是，无论客户需要单核性能还是单插槽性能，威尼斯都是领导者。

512
00:49:18,390 --> 00:49:21,970
And there's one more point that a benchmark doesn't really capture,
还有一点，基准测试其实很难体现，

513
00:49:22,630 --> 00:49:31,010
because when you think about what agentic AI is, it's really like you're adding thousands of employees to your enterprise, to your traditional workflow.
因为当你思考代理式AI时，实际上就像是为企业和传统工作流程增加了数千名员工。

514
00:49:31,770 --> 00:49:35,110
And that software, enterprises have been running on for years.
以及企业多年来一直在运行的软件。

515
00:49:35,790 --> 00:49:39,530
The truth is, that software runs on x86.
事实上，这些软件运行在x86架构上。

516
00:49:40,610 --> 00:49:41,950
So Venice runs all of it.
而威尼斯可以运行所有这些软件。

517
00:49:42,310 --> 00:49:44,330
And this is where x86 has an advantage.
这正是 x86 的优势所在。

518
00:49:44,730 --> 00:49:46,170
You must have the best performance.
你必须拥有最佳性能。

519
00:49:46,370 --> 00:49:47,530
You must have the best density.
你必须拥有最佳密度。

520
00:49:47,970 --> 00:49:51,270
But having that software compatibility is a big, big plus.
但拥有软件兼容性是一个巨大的优势。

521
00:49:51,890 --> 00:49:55,890
So customers scale up their agents on the stack that they already have.
因此，客户可以在他们现有的系统上扩展其代理。

522
00:49:56,870 --> 00:49:59,710
And now, let me just show you what that means at the rack level.
现在，让我来展示一下这在机架层面意味着什么。

523
00:50:00,230 --> 00:50:04,050
So at the rack level, what we find is density is super important.
在机架层面，我们发现密度至关重要。

524
00:50:04,050 --> 00:50:06,070
Everyone's trying to optimize their data center.
每个人都在优化他们的数据中心。

525
00:50:06,310 --> 00:50:08,170
Everyone's trying to optimize their power envelope.
每个人都在优化他们的功耗范围。

526
00:50:09,070 --> 00:50:15,470
And with Venice, every major server OEM is offering a broad spectrum of racks for agentic AI.
有了 Venice，各大服务器 OEM 都提供了广泛多样的机架，以支持代理式 AI。

527
00:50:16,090 --> 00:50:22,890
So what that means is we have the full spectrum from 25,000 cores to 50,000 cores.
这意味着我们从 25,000 个核心到 50,000 个核心，覆盖了完整范围。

528
00:50:23,190 --> 00:50:25,130
And that's more agents per rack.
这意味着每台机架可以支持更多代理。

529
00:50:25,250 --> 00:50:27,050
And that gives customers the choice.
这为客户提供了选择。

530
00:50:27,950 --> 00:50:29,950
The key is, every data center is different.
关键在于，每个数据中心都各不相同。

531
00:50:30,250 --> 00:50:39,150
And with that, the flexibility allows you to pick the right cooling, the right space requirements for what you're trying to do in your data center.
有了这一点，灵活性使您能够根据数据中心的实际需求，选择合适的冷却方式和空间要求。

532
00:50:39,750 --> 00:50:40,790
So there you have it.
所以，情况就是这样。

533
00:50:41,550 --> 00:50:44,690
Venice, the best server CPU in the industry.
威尼斯，业界最强的服务器CPU。

534
00:50:51,620 --> 00:50:55,480
And I'm very happy to say also today that Venice is in full production.
我很高兴地宣布，今天威尼斯已全面投入生产。

535
00:50:56,200 --> 00:50:57,860
Customer demand is incredible.
客户需求非常强劲。

536
00:50:58,300 --> 00:51:01,160
It's the strongest we've ever seen for a new EPYC generation.
这是我们有史以来见过的最强新代EPYC产品需求。

537
00:51:06,990 --> 00:51:18,830
We're seeing every major server OEM, every major cloud provider on track to begin rolling out in the fourth quarter as we start with making the broadest EPYC launch we've ever had.
我们看到所有主要服务器OEM厂商和主要云服务提供商都已按计划，将在第四季度开始推出，而我们将开启有史以来最广泛的EPYC发布。

538
00:51:19,450 --> 00:51:26,370
So with that, I want to turn to my next guest, who runs some of the largest and most advanced compute infrastructure in the world.
接下来，我想介绍下一位嘉宾，他负责管理世界上最大、最先进的计算基础设施之一。

539
00:51:26,810 --> 00:51:33,570
And it's really been our privilege to partner with them as they've deployed multiple generations of both EPYC and Instinct.
我们非常荣幸能与他们合作，见证他们部署了多代EPYC和Instinct产品。

540
00:51:34,070 --> 00:51:40,630
To share more about our work together, please welcome to the stage Meta's Head of Infrastructure, Santosh Janardhan.
为了进一步分享我们合作的成果，请欢迎Meta基础设施负责人桑托什·贾纳德汉登台。

541
00:51:50,750 --> 00:51:52,330
It is so great to have you here.
很高兴你们能来到这里。

542
00:51:52,470 --> 00:51:53,410
Thank you for being here.
感谢你们的到来。

543
00:51:54,550 --> 00:51:56,230
Santosh is a true friend.
桑托什是一位真正的朋友。

544
00:51:56,830 --> 00:52:01,030
I have to say it's been a tremendous opportunity over the last few years.
我必须说，过去几年里这是一次非凡的机会。

545
00:52:01,470 --> 00:52:04,750
My story about Santosh is the first time I sat in his office.
我和桑托什的故事，是我第一次坐在他的办公室里。

546
00:52:05,410 --> 00:52:09,350
He said to me, Lisa, we're going to deploy a lot of CPUs.
他对我说，丽莎，我们要部署大量CPU。

