00:52:18,990 --> 00:52:24,630
But look, Santosh, Meta operates, you operate some of the most advanced infrastructure in the world.
但你看，桑托什，Meta在运营，你们也在运营着世界上一些最先进的基础设施。

552
00:52:26,110 --> 00:52:27,750
What's happening in the data center world?
数据中心领域正在发生什么？

553
00:52:27,810 --> 00:52:28,710
What's happening in your world?
你的世界里发生了什么？

554
00:52:28,810 --> 00:52:33,350
Tell us a little bit about the architecture and what you're working on.
请简单介绍一下架构以及你正在做的工作。

555
00:52:33,810 --> 00:52:34,770
Sure. First of all, thank you.
当然。首先，谢谢。

556
00:52:34,870 --> 00:52:35,370
It's awesome.
太棒了。

557
00:52:35,590 --> 00:52:37,750
This is like a hardware geek's paradise, right?
这简直就像硬件极客的天堂，对吧？

558
00:52:38,170 --> 00:52:42,430
You come in, you're talking about transistors, you're talking about hardware, talking about cooling.
你一进来，就在聊晶体管，聊硬件，聊散热。

559
00:52:42,790 --> 00:52:43,610
This is sort of the gem.
这才是真正的亮点。

560
00:52:43,690 --> 00:52:44,190
I like it.
我喜欢。

561
00:52:45,250 --> 00:52:47,950
And I think there's an audience that's receptive to it.
我觉得有一群观众是愿意接受这些内容的。

562
00:52:48,250 --> 00:52:49,650
I usually talk to audiences.
我通常会面对观众演讲。

563
00:52:50,170 --> 00:52:54,070
They have usually either not been to a data center or not really seen a chip ever.
他们通常要么没去过数据中心，要么根本没见过芯片。

564
00:52:54,450 --> 00:52:56,330
So this is refreshing, I have to say.
所以这让人耳目一新，我必须这么说。

565
00:52:57,470 --> 00:52:58,810
The thing I'll say about...
我想说的是……

566
00:52:58,810 --> 00:53:01,750
Listen, we are seeing demand go through the roof.
听着，我们正看到需求飙升。

567
00:53:02,590 --> 00:53:07,030
When you look at inference, training, recommendation system, that's how a newsfeed works.
从推理、训练、推荐系统来看，这就是新闻推送的工作原理。

568
00:53:08,010 --> 00:53:08,790
Content creation.
内容创作。

569
00:53:09,390 --> 00:53:11,870
The demand for that is just exponential right now.
目前对这方面的需求正呈指数级增长。

570
00:53:12,650 --> 00:53:15,870
And when I think about sort of the overall...
当我思考整体情况时……

571
00:53:17,170 --> 00:53:22,190
Mark has this vision of delivering personal super intelligence to billions of people.
马克有一个愿景，就是为数十亿人提供个人超级智能。

572
00:53:22,430 --> 00:53:33,910
So if you go to sort of Facebook or Instagram or WhatsApp or whatever surface you go to, the idea is that we'll meet you there and we'll deliver super personalized intelligence right wherever you are.
所以无论你去的是 Facebook、Instagram 还是 WhatsApp，或者任何其他平台，我们的想法都是在你所在的地方与你相遇，为你提供高度个性化的超级智能。

573
00:53:34,170 --> 00:53:39,750
And that's why we established this Meta compute initiative and because it's a top level thing, Mark himself oversees.
这就是我们设立 Meta 计算计划的原因，而且这是最高优先级的事项，由马克本人亲自负责。

574
00:53:39,750 --> 00:53:46,770
Now what it means is that we are now moving away from an area where we used to take servers, optimize it.
现在这意味着我们正从过去那种方式转变，我们过去会采购服务器并进行优化。

575
00:53:47,030 --> 00:53:53,490
This is what the conversation we were having many years ago, that, hey, I'm deploying a CPU, I really need to maximize performance out of it.
这就是多年前我们讨论过的内容，当时我说，我正在部署 CPU，真的需要最大化它的性能。

576
00:53:53,650 --> 00:53:54,650
It's different now.
现在情况不同了。

577
00:53:54,990 --> 00:53:58,970
You talked about how we should be thinking about the whole system end to end.
你们谈到了我们应该如何从头到尾地思考整个系统。

578
00:53:59,270 --> 00:54:05,330
We are at a point where we have to look about the whole data center and think about it as one integrated system.
我们现在处于一个必须全面审视整个数据中心，并将其视为一个集成系统的阶段。

579
00:54:05,890 --> 00:54:10,790
Servers, hardware, networking, cooling, power, all of that is not optional.
服务器、硬件、网络、冷却、供电等，这些都不是可选项。

580
00:54:10,830 --> 00:54:12,090
All of that has to work together.
所有这些都必须协同工作。

581
00:54:12,670 --> 00:54:21,910
And this is where I think there's a huge opportunity for collaboration with partners like AMD because you have to now co-design, co-create systems, not just
我认为这正是我们与 AMD 这类合作伙伴开展深度协作的巨大机遇，因为现在你必须共同设计、共同创造系统，而不仅仅是

582
00:54:21,910 --> 00:54:24,290
deploy something that comes off the shelf.
部署一个现成的方案。

583
00:54:25,130 --> 00:54:27,070
The other thing is, by the way, flexibility.
另外，灵活性也很重要。

584
00:54:27,450 --> 00:54:33,950
The thing I really like about what you said is that this is such a big opportunity in the industry right now.
我非常认同你所说的，目前这个行业正面临如此巨大的机遇。

585
00:54:34,110 --> 00:54:37,450
All of us need to lean in and work on this together.
我们所有人都需要积极投入，共同推进。

586
00:54:37,450 --> 00:54:39,650
So it needs to be open.
因此，它必须是开放的。

587
00:54:39,930 --> 00:54:41,010
It needs to be heterogeneous.
它必须是异构的。

588
00:54:41,950 --> 00:54:46,930
And I think that's not one company, one partner that works for any one of us.
我认为这对任何一方来说，都不是某一家公司或某一个合作伙伴就能单独实现的。

589
00:54:47,030 --> 00:54:48,810
We need to sort of work on this together.
我们需要一起在这方面努力。

590
00:54:49,030 --> 00:54:52,550
And that's why I think you're one of our most important strategic partners.
这就是为什么我认为你是我们最重要的战略合作伙伴之一。

591
00:54:53,030 --> 00:54:53,710
Thank you, Santosh.
谢谢你，桑托什。

592
00:54:53,770 --> 00:54:57,030
And look, we completely agree with your philosophy.
而且，我们完全认同你们的理念。

593
00:54:57,490 --> 00:55:07,670
Now, you are actually one of our broadest partners because if you think about our work on CPUs, GPUs, you know, we developed the Rackscale OCP systems together.
现在，实际上你是我们的广泛合作伙伴之一，因为你们想想我们在 CPU 和 GPU 上的工作，我们共同开发了机架规模的 OCP 系统。

594
00:55:08,370 --> 00:55:11,750
You've deployed lots and lots of CPUs, so millions of CPUs.
你们部署了大量 CPU，数以百万计的 CPU。

595
00:55:12,310 --> 00:55:14,670
And you're a lead partner on Venice.
你们是威尼斯项目的牵头合作伙伴。

596
00:55:14,950 --> 00:55:18,610
Can you just talk a little bit about sort of your CPU and infrastructure and some of our work together?
你能简单谈一下你们的 CPU 和基础设施，以及我们之间的合作吗？

597
00:55:19,430 --> 00:55:20,910
Sure. It's been many years.
当然。已经有很多年了。

598
00:55:21,390 --> 00:55:23,930
And the story that Lisa was saying was many years ago.
丽莎刚才说的故事是很多年前的事了。

599
00:55:23,970 --> 00:55:28,490
I think we went from Milan to Bergamo to Turin, now to Venice.
我觉得我们从米兰，到贝加莫，再到都灵，现在到了威尼斯。

600
00:55:28,870 --> 00:55:30,950
So it's at least the fourth generation.
所以至少已经是第四代了。

601
00:55:30,950 --> 00:55:33,530
So a long-time partnership, obviously.
所以这是一段长期的合作，显而易见。

602
00:55:34,270 --> 00:55:38,790
I actually think the world is changing in the sense that it used...
我实际上认为世界正在发生变化，这种变化体现在它开始……

603
00:55:38,790 --> 00:55:39,350
The world is changing.
世界正在发生变化。

604
00:55:39,350 --> 00:55:40,710
Every year is a new world these days.
如今，每年都是一个全新的世界。

605
00:55:40,990 --> 00:55:41,650
It's like every month.
就像每个月一样。

606
00:55:42,510 --> 00:55:43,010
Months, exactly.
每个月，正是如此。

607
00:55:43,370 --> 00:55:46,870
So what ends up happening now is that it's not just a GPU game anymore.
所以现在发生的情况是，这已经不再只是GPU的游戏了。

608
00:55:46,970 --> 00:55:48,270
It's CPUs and GPUs.
这涉及CPU和GPU。

609
00:55:48,430 --> 00:55:52,170
If anything, I think CPUs are becoming at least as important, if not more.
说到底，我认为CPU的重要性至少与GPU相当，甚至可能更重要。

610
00:55:52,570 --> 00:56:04,270
You're looking at a world where sort of the workload is changing because while you have your workhorses and GPUs, at the end of the day, there's agentic workloads.
你面对的是一个工作负载正在变化的世界，因为尽管你有主力的CPU和GPU，但最终仍存在代理型工作负载。

611
00:56:04,270 --> 00:56:05,210
You have to run your tools.
你必须运行你的工具。

612
00:56:05,410 --> 00:56:06,250
You have to run your systems.
你必须运行你的系统。

613
00:56:06,550 --> 00:56:10,590
And all the code that's been generated still needs to run somewhere, right?
所有生成的代码仍然需要在某个地方运行，对吧？

614
00:56:10,810 --> 00:56:12,850
So I'm super excited to work on Venice.
所以我非常期待能参与威尼斯项目。

615
00:56:12,990 --> 00:56:15,270
I think there's a lot to come there.
我觉得那里还有很多值得期待的进展。

616
00:56:15,870 --> 00:56:18,130
And you have to think again.
你必须重新思考一下。

617
00:56:18,790 --> 00:56:26,050
This is a theme that I'm assuming will go throughout the presentation that you have to start thinking about CPUs and GPUs as conjoined things.
这是一个贯穿整个演示的主题，即你需要开始把 CPU 和 GPU 当作协同工作的整体来考虑。

618
00:56:26,050 --> 00:56:27,210
You hand off workloads.
你将工作负载进行移交。

619
00:56:27,210 --> 00:56:29,730
Depending on the workload, you employ the right hardware.
根据工作负载的不同，使用合适的硬件。

620
00:56:30,150 --> 00:56:31,670
Yes, absolutely right.
是的，完全正确。

621
00:56:31,850 --> 00:56:34,550
And we've gotten a lot of feedback from your technical team.
我们收到了你们技术团队的大量反馈。

622
00:56:34,590 --> 00:56:38,990
I think that's what I really appreciate about the partnership with Meta.
我真的很欣赏与 Meta 的合作关系。

623
00:56:39,490 --> 00:56:43,430
Now, clearly, you're deploying lots of GPUs too, a lot of accelerators.
显然，你们也在大规模部署 GPU 和大量加速器。

624
00:56:43,770 --> 00:56:48,970
And you're also one of our deepest partners on the accelerator side, starting with MI300.
而且你们也是我们在加速器领域最深入的合作伙伴之一，从 MI300 开始。

625
00:56:49,290 --> 00:56:56,770
And then we had a very large strategic partnership announced around up to 6 gigawatts, starting with MI450.
然后我们宣布了一项非常重大的战略合作，规模高达6吉瓦，从MI450开始。

626
00:56:57,590 --> 00:56:59,430
And what we're doing is quite unique with Meta.
我们与Meta的合作方式相当独特。

627
00:56:59,530 --> 00:57:04,870
So can you talk a little bit about the evolution and the MI450 plans?
所以你能谈谈MI450的发展历程和相关计划吗？

628
00:57:06,210 --> 00:57:08,190
Again, multi-year collaboration.
这是一次多年期的合作。

629
00:57:08,390 --> 00:57:09,870
I think we started with MI300.
我们最初是从MI300开始的。

630
00:57:10,570 --> 00:57:11,070
We did a bunch.
我们做了很多工作。

631
00:57:11,430 --> 00:57:12,930
It had really nice memory capacity.
它拥有非常出色的内存容量。

632
00:57:13,030 --> 00:57:14,470
I remember talking to you about that, right?
我记得我们曾讨论过这一点，对吧？

633
00:57:15,110 --> 00:57:17,270
And then there's a bunch of pipelining we did.
我们还进行了大量流水线优化。

634
00:57:17,590 --> 00:57:23,730
It was important to just have deployed that at production scale, sort of get hands-on experience on both sides.
重要的是，我们已将它部署到生产规模，双方都获得了实际操作经验。

635
00:57:24,490 --> 00:57:28,170
350 is the first time we deployed this on our ranking and recommendation systems.
MI350是我们在排名和推荐系统中首次部署该技术。

636
00:57:28,310 --> 00:57:32,070
So that's now getting into sort of some good numbers.
现在，数据已经变得相当可观了。

637
00:57:32,550 --> 00:57:34,750
And 450 is, I think, I'm super excited about it.
450让我非常兴奋，我觉得太棒了。

638
00:57:34,850 --> 00:57:36,430
We just got some of the racks.
我们刚刚拿到了一些机架。

639
00:57:36,710 --> 00:57:43,630
And we are going to deploy it across the board because it gives us the opportunity to go and sort of really collaborate.
我们将全面部署，因为这给了我们机会去真正协作。

640
00:57:43,790 --> 00:57:54,650
I think the big difference between the 300, 350, and 450 is that we have had engineers sitting in the same room talking to each other, co-designing, co-creating, like power cooling.
我认为300、350和450之间的主要区别在于，我们有工程师在同一间房里面对面交流，共同设计、共同创造，比如电源和散热。

641
00:57:55,370 --> 00:57:57,370
Like I was saying, it's not just a single thing.
就像我说的，这不仅仅是一个单一的东西。

642
00:57:57,790 --> 00:58:00,250
And we are not shy in feedback.
我们并不回避反馈。

643
00:58:00,490 --> 00:58:01,970
They're not shy, for sure.
他们当然也不回避。

644
00:58:02,990 --> 00:58:04,050
But you're very receptive.
但你们非常乐于接受。

645
00:58:04,230 --> 00:58:05,870
So this is true partnership, right?
所以这才是真正的合作关系，对吧？

646
00:58:06,130 --> 00:58:09,210
This is the point about co-designing and co-creating that, I think.
这就是共同设计和共同创造的意义所在，我认为。

647
00:58:10,150 --> 00:58:14,030
And like I was saying, that's a huge sort of deployment coming in.
就像我说的，这将带来大规模的部署。

648
00:58:14,410 --> 00:58:18,430
The more we deploy, the earlier we co-design, the better we are.
我们部署得越多，越早开始共同设计，我们的表现就越好。

649
00:58:18,630 --> 00:58:19,350
Yeah, absolutely.
是的，绝对的。

650
00:58:19,550 --> 00:58:22,950
Really, really appreciate the effort together on MI450.
真的非常感谢大家在MI450项目上的共同努力。

651
00:58:23,450 --> 00:58:26,150
Now I want to ask you also about your crystal ball.
现在我还想问问你关于你的水晶球。

652
00:58:26,250 --> 00:58:34,150
So you look out into the future and you see what the next few years really means as you push forward in the AI industry.
所以你展望未来，看到在推动AI行业发展过程中，未来几年真正意味着什么。

653
00:58:34,590 --> 00:58:37,870
What are the biggest challenges and really opportunities for us?
我们面临的最大挑战和真正机遇是什么？

654
00:58:38,010 --> 00:58:39,830
This is the industry ecosystem here.
这就是这里的产业生态系统。

655
00:58:39,830 --> 00:58:41,770
So what should we be focused on as an industry?
所以作为整个行业，我们应该关注什么？

656
00:58:42,710 --> 00:58:45,110
Listen, all of you know about the bottlenecks.
听着，你们所有人都知道这些瓶颈。

657
00:58:45,110 --> 00:58:48,310
You know about the power, the data centers, the silicon.
你们知道电力、数据中心、硅材料。

658
00:58:48,870 --> 00:58:52,870
All of these, I think, are choke points that I think the industry is waiting on.
所有这些，我认为都是行业正在等待突破的瓶颈。

659
00:58:53,490 --> 00:58:56,950
But those are things I'm pretty confident we'll sort of work our way through.
但这些事情，我相当有信心我们会逐步解决。

660
00:58:57,250 --> 00:58:59,890
At the end of the day, I think the demand is immense.
归根结底，我认为需求是巨大的。

661
00:59:00,070 --> 00:59:00,850
People are responding.
人们正在作出回应。

662
00:59:01,770 --> 00:59:08,550
But the thing that I really want to make sure all of us realize is that we should not think about systems in isolation.
但我真正希望我们所有人都能意识到的是，我们不应该孤立地看待系统。

663
00:59:09,510 --> 00:59:12,170
Like I was saying, CPUs and GPUs are one conjoined system.
就像我刚才说的，CPU 和 GPU 是一个整体系统。

664
00:59:12,270 --> 00:59:13,730
We should start thinking about it that way.
我们应该这样来思考。

665
00:59:13,730 --> 00:59:18,090
We really need to co-design things early.
我们真的需要尽早进行协同设计。

666
00:59:18,750 --> 00:59:20,190
See, data centers take years to build.
数据中心的建设需要数年时间。

667
00:59:21,350 --> 00:59:26,230
One of my favorite stories is Mark comes to me and says, hey, I want a gigawatt worth of data centers.
我最喜欢的一个故事是，马克来找我，说嘿，我想建一个吉瓦级别的数据中心。

668
00:59:26,350 --> 00:59:27,910
Well, you should have talked to me two years ago.
你两年前就应该和我谈了。

669
00:59:28,510 --> 00:59:29,450
It takes time.
这需要时间。

670
00:59:29,830 --> 00:59:31,270
It's the same with silicon, right?
硅片也是如此，对吧？

671
00:59:31,350 --> 00:59:32,410
It just takes time.
这同样需要时间。

672
00:59:32,950 --> 00:59:39,730
So we need to be starting and sitting down in a room co-designing today for what we need to deploy in 27 and 28.
所以我们需要从今天开始坐下来，协同设计，为 2027 年和 2028 年要部署的内容做好准备。

673
00:59:40,550 --> 00:59:44,130
That, I think, is when we truly unlock all sort of powers of the system.
我认为，那时我们才能真正释放系统的全部潜力。

674
00:59:44,550 --> 00:59:45,450
The systems are amazing.
这些系统非常出色。

675
00:59:45,570 --> 00:59:46,770
The specs are amazing, right?
规格非常惊人，对吧？

676
00:59:47,130 --> 00:59:52,810
But think about how much more you can get out of it if you sit in a room and just co-design it today.
但想想看，如果你今天能坐在一个房间里，共同设计它，能获得的提升会有多大。

677
00:59:52,910 --> 00:59:56,110
And in 28, we'll be having much better graphs out there.
到2028年，我们将拥有更出色的图形表现。

678
00:59:57,410 --> 00:59:57,910
Fantastic.
太棒了。

679
00:59:58,090 --> 00:59:59,450
Santosh, I completely agree with you.
桑托什，我完全同意你的看法。

680
00:59:59,850 --> 01:00:01,510
I want to say again, thank you.
我想再次表示感谢。

681
01:00:01,730 --> 01:00:08,850
We are so, so happy with the amazing partnership that we have across the board and, most importantly, with your engineering teams.
我们对全方位的卓越合作感到无比欣喜，尤其是与你们工程团队的合作。

682
01:00:08,870 --> 01:00:11,310
And we truly are excited about what we're going to do in the future.
我们对未来的合作充满期待。

683
01:00:11,750 --> 01:00:12,350
Thank you so much.
非常感谢。

684
01:00:19,000 --> 01:00:26,600
So you heard Santosh talk about just the diversity of workloads and really the massive scale that you require with AI.
所以你们听到了桑托什谈到工作负载的多样性，以及AI所需的巨大规模。

685
01:00:27,420 --> 01:00:32,500
Now I want to turn to another part of the inference market where the requirements are actually very different.
现在我想转向推理市场中的另一个部分，这里的实际需求非常不同。

686
01:00:33,140 --> 01:00:35,140
So lots and lots of workloads.
有很多很多的工作负载。

687
01:00:35,420 --> 01:00:42,440
And as inference is moving into more products and services, we're actually seeing it segment into different workloads depending on what you're trying to do.
随着推理逐渐融入更多产品和服务，我们实际上看到它根据你所要实现的目标，分化为不同类型的工作负载。

688
01:00:43,360 --> 01:00:45,620
Some of these are, let's call it, less interactive.
其中一些可以称为非交互式。

689
01:00:45,620 --> 01:00:49,880
So they're really tuned for, let's call it, maximum throughput or the lowest cost.
它们主要针对的是最大吞吐量或最低成本。

690
01:00:50,900 --> 01:00:56,520
Other of these applications require more balanced throughput, so you have to balance throughput and responsiveness.
其他一些应用则需要更均衡的吞吐量，因此你必须在吞吐量和响应速度之间取得平衡。

691
01:00:57,360 --> 01:01:02,620
And then there's this new class of applications that actually want very, very fast results.
然后还有这一类全新的应用，它们实际上需要非常非常快速的结果。

692
01:01:02,660 --> 01:01:05,760
You have extremely smart engineers and they don't like to wait.
你有极其聪明的工程师，他们不喜欢等待。

693
01:01:06,280 --> 01:01:10,980
And that is where ultra-low latency or every millisecond actually matters.
这正是超低延迟发挥作用的地方，每一毫秒都至关重要。

694
01:01:11,720 --> 01:01:15,640
Each one of these types of workloads requires a different type of compute.
这些不同类型的工作负载需要不同类型的计算。

695
01:01:16,380 --> 01:01:21,700
And one of the best ways to reach ultra-low latency today is disaggregated inference.
如今实现超低延迟的最佳方式之一是解耦推理。

696
01:01:22,220 --> 01:01:28,460
So if you think about the different pieces, both prefill and decode are two different jobs.
所以你如果考虑各个组成部分，预填充和解码是两个不同的任务。

697
01:01:28,720 --> 01:01:30,880
So prefill tends to need more compute.
因此，预填充通常需要更多的计算能力。

698
01:01:31,560 --> 01:01:33,560
Decode tends to need more memory bandwidth.
解码通常需要更高的内存带宽。

699
01:01:34,100 --> 01:01:40,380
And with Instinct, we have a very balanced machine so that we deliver both great compute and great memory bandwidth.
而使用Instinct，我们打造了一台非常均衡的机器，能够同时提供出色的计算能力和出色的内存带宽。

700
01:01:40,840 --> 01:01:42,860
But you can actually take this a step further.
但实际上，你可以更进一步。

701
01:01:42,860 --> 01:01:49,500
If you know what workloads you're trying to run, you can actually let customers tune each of these pieces independently.
如果你知道自己要运行的工作负载，实际上可以让客户独立调整这些各个部分。

702
01:01:49,940 --> 01:01:54,240
And to address this market opportunity, we've been working with Cerebras.
为把握这一市场机遇，我们一直在与Cerebras合作。

703
01:01:54,700 --> 01:02:01,300
So to talk more about what we're building together, please welcome to the stage Cerebras co-founder and CEO Andrew Feldman.
接下来，让我们欢迎Cerebras联合创始人兼CEO安德鲁·菲尔德曼上台，进一步聊聊我们共同打造的产品。

704
01:02:10,330 --> 01:02:11,850
Andrew, it's great to have you here.
安德鲁，欢迎你来到这里。

705
01:02:11,950 --> 01:02:14,070
It's been an exciting few months for you.
这几个月对你来说一定非常激动人心。

706
01:02:14,470 --> 01:02:18,590
I know that for those who don't know exactly what you've been working on,
我知道，对于那些还不清楚你具体在做什么的人，

707
01:02:18,590 --> 01:02:22,490
can you talk a little bit about Cerebras and what problem you've been trying to solve?
你能简单介绍一下Cerebras，以及你们正在解决什么问题吗？

708
01:02:23,050 --> 01:02:27,970
Sure. Great to be here and great to be sort of among people who love hardware.
当然。很高兴来到这里，也很高兴能和一群热爱硬件的人在一起。

709
01:02:28,810 --> 01:02:30,130
Yes, it's nice.
是的，这很棒。

710
01:02:30,650 --> 01:02:37,330
Look, I'm thrilled to be here with you and to announce our cool new partnership.
看，我很高兴能和你们在一起，并宣布我们全新的酷合作。

711
01:02:37,870 --> 01:02:42,190
At Cerebras, we build the world's largest and fastest chip.
在 Cerebras，我们打造世界上最大、最快的大芯片。

712
01:02:42,330 --> 01:02:43,550
It's a full wafer.
这是一整片晶圆。

713
01:02:43,810 --> 01:02:52,450
And we package this into a system into racks and then racks into clusters.
我们将它封装成系统，再装进机架，然后机架组成集群。

714
01:02:53,510 --> 01:02:56,970
And we deliver them both on-premise and via the cloud.
我们既提供本地部署，也通过云服务交付。

715
01:02:57,690 --> 01:03:00,930
And you've had some of our customers up here already today.
今天你们已经见过我们的一些客户了。

716
01:03:01,250 --> 01:03:13,050
On the Frontier Labs, we serve customers like OpenAI and in the hyperscalers like AWS, in the small agentic and the coding space, leaders like Cognition.
在 Frontier 实验室，我们服务的客户包括 OpenAI，以及 AWS 这样的超大规模云服务商，还有在小型代理和编程领域中的领军企业，比如 Cognition。

717
01:03:13,750 --> 01:03:18,350
And they do this because we're blisteringly fast.
他们选择我们，是因为我们速度惊人。

718
01:03:19,790 --> 01:03:25,370
There's no question, Andrew, that you have some tremendous innovation with what you've been working on.
安德鲁，毫无疑问，你在所做项目上的创新非常了不起。

719
01:03:25,650 --> 01:03:34,670
And our teams have been collaborating really closely over the last few years to really have Helios together with the wafer scale engine for ultra low latency inference.
过去几年里，我们的团队紧密合作，终于将 Helios 与晶圆级引擎结合，实现了超低延迟推理。

720
01:03:35,150 --> 01:03:37,570
Can you just kind of just educate the audience a little bit?
你能稍微给观众讲一下吗？

721
01:03:37,630 --> 01:03:39,990
What are we trying to do and what does that mean for customers?
我们正在尝试做什么，这对客户意味着什么？

722
01:03:39,990 --> 01:03:44,250
Sure, I think what's happened, and you described it previously,
当然，我认为发生的情况是，正如你之前描述的那样，

723
01:03:44,530 --> 01:03:51,130
is that sort of AI has moved from being a novelty to being useful and then in some domains a necessity.
人工智能已经从一种新奇事物转变为有用工具，而在某些领域甚至成为必需品。

724
01:03:52,190 --> 01:03:57,710
And when something is a necessity, people want to use it and they want to use it quickly.
当某样东西成为必需品时，人们就希望使用它，并且希望快速使用。

725
01:03:57,910 --> 01:04:09,050
And to serve this market, this segment of ultra low latency, we sought a partnership that could extend our capabilities and our footprint.
为了服务这个超低延迟的市场细分领域，我们寻求了一项能扩展我们能力与覆盖范围的合作伙伴关系。

726
01:04:09,050 --> 01:04:10,970
And there was no better answer than AMD.
没有比 AMD 更合适的答案了。

727
01:04:11,510 --> 01:04:17,930
We were already an AMD customer as we use AMD CPUs to surround our systems.
我们原本就是 AMD 的客户，因为我们使用 AMD 的 CPU 来构建我们的系统。

728
01:04:18,110 --> 01:04:32,650
And we were so excited at the opportunity to build a disaggregated solution that combined AMD CPUs, the cool new Helios rack and the cerebrus wafer scale engine.
我们非常兴奋能有机会打造一个解耦解决方案，将 AMD 的 CPU、全新的 Helios 机架以及 Cerebrus 芯片级封装引擎结合在一起。

729
01:04:33,190 --> 01:04:36,270
Yeah, look, the technology is pretty cool.
是的，这技术确实很酷。

730
01:04:36,270 --> 01:04:38,670
So just talk a little bit about how it comes together.
那就简单说一下它是如何整合在一起的。

731
01:04:38,670 --> 01:04:49,630
Sure. So as Lisa described, what you have with Instinct and the Helios rack is that you have the leader in performance and memory capacity.
好的。正如丽莎所描述的，Instinct 和 Helios 机架的组合，意味着你拥有了性能和内存容量的领导者。

732
01:04:50,130 --> 01:04:57,710
And you marry that with our wafer scale engine, which is the leader in sort of in SRAM and in memory bandwidth.
再与我们的芯片级封装引擎结合，后者在 SRAM 和内存带宽方面处于领先地位。

733
01:04:58,490 --> 01:05:04,010
And that combination allows us to deliver a solution that is unmatched in the industry.
这种组合使我们能够提供业界无与伦比的解决方案。

734
01:05:04,950 --> 01:05:05,930
Very, very exciting.
非常非常令人兴奋。

735
01:05:06,050 --> 01:05:08,950
I know that customers are excited about what we're going to do together as well.
我知道客户也对我们将要共同完成的事情充满期待。

736
01:05:09,330 --> 01:05:11,390
So when are we going to have it in market?
那么我们什么时候才能在市场上看到它？

737
01:05:12,950 --> 01:05:13,990
Later this year.
今年晚些时候。

738
01:05:14,290 --> 01:05:23,670
It will be first in the cerebrus cloud and it will be later at a store near you.
它将首先在Cerebrus云中推出，随后很快就会在您附近的门店上线。

739
01:05:25,230 --> 01:05:32,750
I think the key thing is we're going to give customers a choice to really put together what is the solution that they want.
我认为关键在于，我们将为客户提供选择，真正让他们打造自己想要的解决方案。

740
01:05:32,850 --> 01:05:35,690
And I think we're very, very happy to be able to do this together with you.
我认为我们非常高兴能与你们一起实现这一点。

741
01:05:35,690 --> 01:05:40,630
So I think it's a huge step up in terms of what we can do for this ultra low latency segment.
所以我认为，这在应对超低延迟领域方面是一个巨大的飞跃。

742
01:05:40,830 --> 01:05:41,510
I think that's right.
我认为没错。

743
01:05:41,650 --> 01:05:50,630
I think until recently, customers sort of, they could have sort of high throughput or they could have extraordinary speed.
我认为直到最近，客户只能在高吞吐量和超高速之间二选一。

744
01:05:50,650 --> 01:05:56,470
And by bringing together the Helios rack with the cerebrus wafer scale engine,
通过将Helios机架与Cerebrus晶圆级引擎结合在一起，

745
01:05:56,730 --> 01:06:03,790
we give you five times the throughput while continuing to deliver this extraordinary speed.
我们在保持卓越速度的同时，将吞吐量提升了五倍。

746
01:06:03,790 --> 01:06:07,010
It's really something amazing.
这真的令人惊叹。

747
01:06:07,810 --> 01:06:08,110
Fantastic.
太棒了。

748
01:06:08,010 --> 01:06:12,630
Well, look, Andrew, huge congratulations to what you and the Cerebras team have done.
嗯，安德鲁，恭喜你和Cerebras团队所取得的成就。

749
01:06:12,630 --> 01:06:13,670
I mean, I think it's been incredible.
我觉得这简直难以置信。

750
01:06:13,850 --> 01:06:17,150
I think you've been clear on what you're trying to accomplish.
我认为你很清楚自己想要实现的目标。

751
01:06:17,430 --> 01:06:25,310
And it's really nice to see not only it come together, but us come together to offer a solution that will be very, very compelling to customers.
看到它最终成型，也看到我们携手合作，提供一个对客户极具吸引力的解决方案，这感觉非常好。

752
01:06:25,330 --> 01:06:27,310
So we can't wait to get this into customers' hands.
我们迫不及待想把产品交到客户手中。

753
01:06:27,790 --> 01:06:29,190
Soon. Thank you.
不久之后。谢谢。

754
01:06:29,190 --> 01:06:29,630
Good to see you.
很高兴见到你。

755
01:06:29,630 --> 01:06:30,250
Thank you so much.
非常感谢。

756
01:06:30,470 --> 01:06:30,990
Thank you, Andrew.
谢谢你，安德鲁。

757
01:06:36,240 --> 01:06:36,960
Alright.
好的。

758
01:06:37,180 --> 01:06:40,120
So look, I think we've shown you a lot of hardware this morning.
所以，我想我们今天早上已经向大家展示了大量的硬件。

759
01:06:41,300 --> 01:06:43,640
But as we all know, hardware is only part of the story.
但正如我们所知，硬件只是故事的一部分。

760
01:06:44,260 --> 01:06:49,380
It's actually software that turns all of this into a platform that developers can really build on.
真正让这一切变成开发者可以真正基于其构建的平台的，其实是软件。

761
01:06:49,820 --> 01:06:56,720
So to share the progress we're making with ROCm, please welcome AMD Senior Vice President of AI, Vamsi Boppana, to the stage.
为了分享我们在 ROCm 方面取得的进展，请欢迎 AMD 人工智能高级副总裁瓦姆西·博帕纳登台。

762
01:07:03,870 --> 01:07:04,710
Thank you, Lisa.
谢谢，丽莎。

763
01:07:04,810 --> 01:07:05,810
Good morning, everyone.
大家早上好。

764
01:07:06,350 --> 01:07:06,870
Good morning.
早上好。

765
01:07:07,410 --> 01:07:09,750
It's great to be back to talk about software.
很高兴再次来谈论软件。

766
01:07:09,750 --> 01:07:16,690
Just a few years ago, programming AMD GPUs required deep expertise and significant engineering effort.
几年前，编程 AMD 显卡需要深厚的专业知识和大量的工程投入。

767
01:07:17,150 --> 01:07:21,100
We've come a long, long way in a remarkably short period of time.
我们在短短的很短时间内，已经走了很长一段路。

768
01:07:21,370 --> 01:07:31,290
Through our open source community collaboration and sustained investment in ROCm, our software stack, AMD Instinct GPUs are powering some of the most
通过我们开源社区的合作以及对 ROCm 的持续投入，我们的软件栈使 AMD Instinct 显卡正在推动一些最

769
01:07:31,290 --> 01:07:34,870
important and consequential workloads on the planet.
地球上最重要且影响深远的工作负载。

770
01:07:35,330 --> 01:07:38,530
But the biggest change is still ahead of us.
但最大的变革仍在未来等待着我们。

771
01:07:38,530 --> 01:07:46,030
AI is transforming how software is getting built, and we are bringing that transformation to ROCm.
人工智能正在改变软件的构建方式，而我们正将这一变革带到 ROCm。

772
01:07:46,590 --> 01:07:48,650
And that's what I'm excited to share with you guys today.
这就是我今天想与大家分享的内容。

773
01:07:49,690 --> 01:07:53,370
Our software teams have been moving fast with relentless focus on developers.
我们的软件团队一直以极快的速度推进，始终专注于开发者。

774
01:07:54,330 --> 01:08:00,250
We've invested at every level of the stack in build and test infrastructure so we ship faster.
我们在堆栈的每个层面都投入了资源，完善构建和测试基础设施，以实现更快的交付。

775
01:08:01,270 --> 01:08:06,010
ROCm releases now go out every six weeks, not every four months.
ROCm 现在每六周发布一次，而不是每四个月一次。

776
01:08:06,010 --> 01:08:10,610
We've continued to expand the work we do with our AI ecosystem partners.
我们持续扩大与 AI 生态合作伙伴的合作范围。

777
01:08:11,170 --> 01:08:11,730
And the result?
结果如何？

778
01:08:12,650 --> 01:08:18,150
More features, faster performance, and a significantly better out-of-the-box experience.
功能更多，性能更快，开箱即用的体验显著提升。

779
01:08:19,290 --> 01:08:23,810
Our strategy that has gotten us here has been remarkably consistent.
带领我们走到今天的战略，一直非常一致。

780
01:08:24,350 --> 01:08:25,990
It's built on two core principles.
它建立在两个核心原则之上。

781
01:08:27,370 --> 01:08:35,050
Partner deeply with the open source ecosystem and build with the right layers of abstraction to enable developer productivity.
与开源生态系统深度合作，构建合适的抽象层级，以提升开发人员的生产力。

782
01:08:35,050 --> 01:08:42,070
Open source gives us velocity and scale, and abstraction makes developers more productive.
开源赋予我们速度与规模，而抽象则让开发人员更加高效。

783
01:08:44,210 --> 01:08:50,430
Our deep, deep commitment to open source has resonated with the community that has truly embraced AMD.
我们对开源的深切承诺已深深打动社区，AMD也真正获得了社区的接纳。

784
01:08:51,210 --> 01:08:55,070
From frameworks and compiler stacks to inference engines and model hubs,
从框架和编译器栈，到推理引擎和模型库，

785
01:08:55,070 --> 01:09:06,950
AMD is now becoming part of default enablement for the most important AI communities, such as Hugging Face, PyTorch, JAX, vLLM, and SGLang.
AMD如今已成为最重要的AI社区（如Hugging Face、PyTorch、JAX、vLLM和SGLang）的默认支持平台。

786
01:09:07,510 --> 01:09:14,590
This is why new models get Day Zero support and why the world's most important AI workloads run on AMD today.
这正是新模型能获得Day Zero支持的原因，也是当今全球最重要的AI工作负载运行在AMD上的原因。

787
01:09:14,950 --> 01:09:16,990
That is a big shift.
这是一个巨大的转变。

788
01:09:17,930 --> 01:09:24,610
Inspired by engineers seeking productivity, abstractions have evolved to enable work at the right level of detail.
受追求生产力的工程师启发，抽象层级不断演进，使人们能够在合适的细节层次上开展工作。

789
01:09:24,610 --> 01:09:31,010
Hiding complexity when they want speed, and exposing control when they need performance.
需要速度时隐藏复杂性，需要性能时则暴露控制权。

790
01:09:31,830 --> 01:09:40,610
From low-level programming in assembly and C to block programming abstractions like Triton to Pythonic frameworks, we've invested in key abstractions.
从汇编和C语言的底层编程，到Triton等块级编程抽象，再到Python风格的框架，我们已在关键抽象上投入大量资源。

791
01:09:41,790 --> 01:09:49,790
Aiter, our kernel library, and Atom, our serving engine, get you peak performance without writing the kernels yourself.
Aiter是我们自己的内核库，Atom是我们的推理引擎，无需自行编写内核即可获得峰值性能。

792
01:09:51,230 --> 01:09:59,310
FlyDSL is a brand new Pythonic domain-specific language that gives you low-level control with the performance of hand-tuned C++.
FlyDSL是一种全新的Python风格领域特定语言，让你在获得手调C++性能的同时，拥有底层控制力。

793
01:10:00,370 --> 01:10:07,970
And Mori, our communications library, helps deliver leadership performance on the latest models, like Minimax.
而且，我们的通信库Mori，帮助我们在最新模型（如Minimax）上实现卓越的领导力表现。

794
01:10:09,790 --> 01:10:12,770
But look, something very, very exciting is happening.
但看吧，正在发生一件非常、非常令人兴奋的事。

795
01:10:13,430 --> 01:10:16,590
Over the past year, I've seen something remarkable inside AMD.
过去一年里，我在AMD内部见证了一些非凡的进展。

796
01:10:16,590 --> 01:10:24,770
Our engineers are using AI models to generate GPU kernels, optimize code, debug issues, and improve performance.
我们的工程师正在使用AI模型生成GPU内核、优化代码、调试问题并提升性能。

797
01:10:25,050 --> 01:10:29,050
And in some cases, these AI-generated kernels are shockingly good.
在某些情况下，这些由AI生成的内核表现得令人震惊。

798
01:10:29,930 --> 01:10:31,430
Better than what we expected.
比我们预期的还要好。

799
01:10:31,910 --> 01:10:35,510
Sometimes better than the most manually-tuned versions.
有时甚至优于那些手工精心调优的版本。

800
01:10:36,130 --> 01:10:38,570
The first time you see this, you're a little bit skeptical.
第一次看到这种情况时，你难免会有些怀疑。

801
01:10:39,430 --> 01:10:46,330
You run more tests, you try to break it, you look for what went wrong, and then you realize this is real.
你会进行更多测试，试图找出问题，寻找出错的地方，然后才意识到这确实是真实的。

802
01:10:46,330 --> 01:10:53,930
What has happened in general software development is coming to significantly transform GPU programming.
通用软件开发中发生的变化，正在显著改变GPU编程。

803
01:10:54,110 --> 01:11:03,730
It's going to reduce the time it takes to bring up workloads, make optimization automated, and it will remove any remaining barriers to broad adoption.
这将缩短部署工作负载所需的时间，实现优化自动化，并消除广泛采用的任何剩余障碍。

804
01:11:04,630 --> 01:11:09,850
We want to put that capability in the hands of every developer.
我们希望将这种能力赋予每一位开发者。

805
01:11:09,850 --> 01:11:15,110
So today, I am excited to introduce ROCm.ai.
今天，我非常激动地向大家介绍 ROCm.ai。

806
01:11:22,210 --> 01:11:28,510
It's an agentic AI platform that brings the capabilities of AI-assisted GPU programming to developers.
它是一个智能AI平台，将AI辅助GPU编程的能力带给开发者。

807
01:11:29,150 --> 01:11:37,690
It starts with the simple idea of giving developers access to the power of an AMD ecosystem through the AI coding agents they already use.
这个平台始于一个简单理念：让开发者通过他们已使用的AI编码代理，访问AMD生态系统的强大能力。

808
01:11:37,690 --> 01:11:50,450
Whether you're using Cursor, Claude, Codex, rocm.ai helps those agents understand AMD platforms, understand ROCm, and helps you build and optimize your workloads.
无论你使用的是 Cursor、Claude、Codex，ROCm.ai 都能帮助这些代理理解AMD平台、理解ROCm，并帮助你构建和优化工作负载。

809
01:11:50,850 --> 01:11:56,850
In other words, we are making those popular coding agents into ROCm super users.
换句话说，我们正在把那些流行的编码代理变成ROCm的超级用户。

810
01:11:57,170 --> 01:12:03,730
You should be able to describe the workload you want to run, the performance target you want to hit, and then let the agents help you get there.
你应该能够描述你想要运行的工作负载、想要达到的性能目标，然后让这些代理帮你实现。

811
01:12:04,910 --> 01:12:08,490
For years, we have been building the open software foundation.
多年来，我们一直在构建开放软件基础。

812
01:12:09,030 --> 01:12:16,370
Now, we are adding an AI-assisted layer that helps developers use that foundation faster and more effectively.
现在，我们增加了一个AI辅助层，帮助开发者更快、更高效地使用这一基础。

813
01:12:16,790 --> 01:12:19,050
So let me show you what is inside ROCm.ai.
那么，让我来展示一下ROCm.ai内部都有什么。

814
01:12:20,330 --> 01:12:30,730
It's built on the foundational capabilities of ROCm, our core software stack, runtime, libraries, compilers, tools, framework integration, all of the
它建立在ROCm的基础能力之上，包括我们核心的软件栈、运行时、库、编译器、工具、框架集成，以及所有让这一栈正常运行的核心软件。

815
01:12:30,730 --> 01:12:32,450
core software that makes the stack work.
核心软件使整个栈得以运行。

816
01:12:32,450 --> 01:12:39,050
On top of that, we built a layer of AI-assisted optimization called Hyperloom.
在此基础上，我们构建了一个名为Hyperloom的AI辅助优化层。

817
01:12:40,130 --> 01:12:44,830
Using Hyperloom, the system can analyze the workload, tune configurations,
通过 Hyperloom，系统可以分析工作负载，调整配置，

818
01:12:45,330 --> 01:12:50,550
select and tune kernels, adjust parallelism strategies, and iterate towards performance goals.
选择并优化内核，调整并行策略，并迭代以达成性能目标。

819
01:12:51,610 --> 01:12:57,250
To give you an example of the power of Hyperloom, I was talking to the lead developer last week.
举个 Hyperloom 能力的例子，我上周和首席开发人员聊过。

820
01:12:57,250 --> 01:13:06,390
He told me they just pushed through a suite of 14,000 models through Hyperloom, optimizing them and creating valuable insights.
他告诉我，他们刚刚通过 Hyperloom 推送了 14,000 个模型，进行了优化并获得了有价值的洞察。

821
01:13:06,590 --> 01:13:12,150
This would have been impossible to imagine, even with a large team of engineers before.
即使在拥有大量工程师团队的情况下，这在过去也是难以想象的。

822
01:13:12,570 --> 01:13:13,910
That's the power of Hyperloom.
这就是 Hyperloom 的力量。

823
01:13:14,890 --> 01:13:23,010
And finally, we provide an AI-native interface for our developers, AI skills that allow coding agents to understand ROCm natively.
最后，我们为开发者提供了原生 AI 接口，具备 AI 技能，使编码代理能够原生理解 ROCm。

824
01:13:23,010 --> 01:13:27,050
I'm incredibly excited by what we have built with rocm.ai.
我对与 rocm.ai 一起打造的成果感到无比兴奋。

825
01:13:27,490 --> 01:13:31,810
It's going to profoundly transform the way developers interact with our platforms.
它将深刻改变开发者与我们平台互动的方式。

826
01:13:32,630 --> 01:13:34,870
So let me make this concrete for you with an example.
让我用一个例子来具体说明。

827
01:13:35,890 --> 01:13:41,750
Imagine you are a developer who wants to optimize Minimax M3 with vLLM on MI355s.
想象你是一名开发者，想要在 MI355s 上使用 vLLM 优化 Minimax M3。

828
01:13:42,410 --> 01:13:45,250
Today, there are many things you need to get right.
今天，你需要掌握许多细节才能成功。

829
01:13:45,570 --> 01:13:50,870
You need the right vLLM optimizations, the right model recipes, the right environment variables.
你需要正确的 vLLM 优化、正确的模型配方和正确的环境变量。

830
01:13:50,870 --> 01:13:56,210
You may need to write new kernels or optimize kernels, and then you still need to tune all of this.
你可能需要编写新的内核或优化内核，然后仍然需要对所有这些进行调优。

831
01:13:57,250 --> 01:14:01,530
With rocm.ai, this interaction becomes much simpler.
使用 rocm.ai，这种交互变得简单得多。

832
01:14:02,610 --> 01:14:03,390
So let's see it.
那么我们来看看。

833
01:14:03,470 --> 01:14:07,910
You can say, optimize Minimax M3 with Hyperloom.
你可以输入：使用 Hyperloom 优化 Minimax M3。

834
01:14:08,390 --> 01:14:14,890
Enter. And behind the scenes, the agent does what an expert would do.
按下回车。后台，代理会像专家一样操作。

835
01:14:15,770 --> 01:14:18,830
Pulls a known good recipe, runs and profiles the workload.
调用一个已知可靠的配方，运行并分析工作负载。

836
01:14:18,830 --> 01:14:24,270
It creates and tests a bunch of kernel and runtime configurations, and it keeps iterating towards target.
它会创建并测试大量内核和运行时配置，并持续迭代以达到目标。

837
01:14:25,970 --> 01:14:30,490
You can actually watch on screen here rocm.ai write a GPU kernel.
你实际上可以在这里看到 rocm.ai 编写 GPU 内核的过程。

838
01:14:31,130 --> 01:14:34,530
It sees an opportunity to write a more optimized MOE group gem.
它发现了一个机会，可以编写一个更优化的 MOE 组 gem。

839
01:14:35,890 --> 01:14:36,750
And the result?
结果如何？

840
01:14:37,390 --> 01:14:44,670
rocm.ai delivers a 38% more tokens per second improvement on this specific example.
rocm.ai 在这个具体示例中实现了每秒多处理 38% 词元的提升。

841
01:14:45,110 --> 01:14:47,630
This is the experience we want for developers.
这正是我们希望开发者获得的体验。

842
01:14:47,630 --> 01:14:49,370
Simple to start.
开始使用非常简单。

843
01:14:52,240 --> 01:14:53,540
That's pretty cool, huh?
这挺酷的，对吧？

844
01:14:57,640 --> 01:15:00,100
Simple, simple to start and powerful to optimize.
简单易上手，强大易优化。

845
01:15:00,740 --> 01:15:03,560
We've continued our relentless focus and performance.
我们持续专注于性能提升。

846
01:15:03,920 --> 01:15:07,340
With every release, we've delivered significant performance gains.
每次发布都带来了显著的性能提升。

847
01:15:07,920 --> 01:15:14,120
On leading models like DeepSeek, rocm.ai delivers 3.3 times speed up over ROCm 7.
在 DeepSeek 等领先模型上，rocm.ai 相比 ROCm 7 实现了 3.3 倍的加速。

848
01:15:14,940 --> 01:15:18,260
This has been made possible by innovations at every level of the stack.
这得益于整个技术栈各层面的创新。

849
01:15:18,260 --> 01:15:26,440
Techniques such as the use of block-scaled fused MOE kernels, KV cache quantization, export parallelism.
诸如使用块缩放融合 MOE 内核、KV 缓存量化、导出并行等技术。

850
01:15:26,920 --> 01:15:31,320
But look, the bigger story is how AI agents actually profiled the workload,
但更值得关注的是，AI 代理实际上对工作负载进行了分析，

851
01:15:31,480 --> 01:15:35,980
proposed new kernels, tested configurations, and actually validated all of the results.
提出了新的内核，测试了配置，并验证了所有结果。

852
01:15:37,360 --> 01:15:41,940
That exact same focus is also on delivering performance gains for training.
这种同样的专注也体现在训练性能的提升上。

853
01:15:42,700 --> 01:15:48,240
On the same hardware, rocm.ai improves training performance by an average of 2.4 times.
在相同硬件上，rocm.ai 将训练性能平均提升了 2.4 倍。

854
01:15:48,240 --> 01:15:55,760
Through optimized kernels such as fused flash attention, more efficient checkpointing, and advanced parallelism strategies.
通过优化的内核，例如融合闪存注意力、更高效的检查点机制以及先进的并行策略。

855
01:15:57,320 --> 01:16:03,200
Our engineers have done amazing work to unlock the capabilities of MI455 through rocm.ai.
我们的工程师通过 rocm.ai 完成了令人惊叹的工作，充分释放了 MI455 的潜力。

856
01:16:04,060 --> 01:16:07,060
So I'm delighted to share some incredible results on hardware.
因此，我很高兴能与大家分享一些在硬件上的惊人成果。

857
01:16:08,040 --> 01:16:17,660
On running real workloads, we are able to see the system deliver 20 terabytes of memory bandwidth and 20 petaflops of delivered compute.
在运行真实工作负载时，我们能够看到系统实现了 20TB/s 的内存带宽和 20PFLOPS 的实际计算性能。

858
01:16:17,660 --> 01:16:26,400
These are the highest demonstrated compute plus memory capabilities of any accelerator platform in the industry today.
这是目前行业内任何加速平台所展示出的最高计算与内存能力。

859
01:16:27,100 --> 01:16:28,700
It's not theoretical, there's measured.
这并非理论推测，而是实测数据。

860
01:16:35,380 --> 01:16:37,880
Super exciting that we were able to share this on day one.
我们能在第一天就分享这些成果，令人无比激动。

861
01:16:38,640 --> 01:16:46,420
I'm also thrilled to share that the leading AI ecosystem partners who have had their hands on MI455 have had a delightful experience.
我还非常高兴地宣布，那些已经接触过 MI455 的领先 AI 生态合作伙伴，都体验到了令人愉悦的使用感受。

862
01:16:46,420 --> 01:16:49,100
You can see here what they've had to say.
你们可以在这里看到他们的真实反馈。

863
01:16:49,740 --> 01:16:57,800
From end-to-end PyTorch testing, to ensuring Hugging Face models are getting validated, to vLLM and SGLang running well on MI455.
从端到端的 PyTorch 测试，到确保 Hugging Face 模型得到验证，再到 vLLM 和 SGLang 在 MI455 上运行良好。

864
01:16:58,680 --> 01:17:04,520
We are incredibly encouraged and excited by what the community is about to unlock with MI455.
我们对社区即将通过 MI455 实现的突破感到无比鼓舞和兴奋。

865
01:17:05,280 --> 01:17:12,780
This matters because day zero readiness is one of the most important objectives we strive for, and that's what rocm.ai enables.
这很重要，因为零日就绪是我们努力追求的最重要目标之一，而 rocm.ai 正是实现这一点的关键。

866
01:17:13,680 --> 01:17:17,700
So now let's look at rocm.ai in action on Helios.
现在让我们看看 rocm.ai 在 Helios 上的实际运行情况。

867
01:17:18,160 --> 01:17:20,840
This time we are going to use a Codex front end.
这次我们将使用一个 Codex 前端。

868
01:17:21,300 --> 01:17:27,840
Let's deploy DeepSeek V4 Pro, a 1.6 trillion parameter frontier model on Helios.
我们在 Helios 上部署 DeepSeek V4 Pro，这是一个拥有 1.6 万亿参数的前沿模型。

869
01:17:28,460 --> 01:17:29,680
Now watch what happens.
现在请看发生了什么。

870
01:17:31,400 --> 01:17:42,380
rocm.ai pulls the right recipes, it configures the runtime, it implements the model graph onto hardware, and finally serves up the model.
rocm.ai 自动调用合适的配置方案，配置运行时环境，将模型图映射到硬件，并最终提供模型服务。

871
01:17:43,190 --> 01:17:44,580
There you go.
看到了吗。

872
01:17:44,900 --> 01:17:46,300
The model is actually up and running.
模型实际上已经启动并运行。

873
01:17:47,320 --> 01:17:51,580
And let's see the model write a simple poem now about advancing AI.
现在让我们看看模型如何写一首关于推进 AI 的简单诗歌。

874
01:17:52,780 --> 01:17:53,460
Let's hit enter.
我们按下回车键。

875
01:17:55,400 --> 01:17:56,860
Isn't that a pretty cool poem?
这首诗是不是很酷？

876
01:18:02,070 --> 01:18:04,510
This is the experience we want to give our users.
这正是我们希望为用户带来的体验。

877
01:18:04,930 --> 01:18:13,550
The developers should not have to manually reason through every layer of model architecture, kernel selection, COM strategy, and rack level deployment.
开发人员不应再手动分析模型架构的每一层、内核选择、COM 策略以及机架级部署的细节。

878
01:18:13,550 --> 01:18:20,850
AI is transforming this experience, and that is a very, very big shift for GPU hardware and software.
人工智能正在改变这一体验，这对 GPU 硬件和软件而言是一次非常巨大的转变。

879
01:18:22,330 --> 01:18:27,010
Now, there are few organizations shaping the frontier of AI as much as OpenAI.
目前，很少有组织能像 OpenAI 一样推动人工智能的前沿发展。

880
01:18:27,450 --> 01:18:30,390
You heard Lisa and Sachin talk about our partnership.
你们已经听到丽莎和萨钦谈过我们的合作。

881
01:18:30,790 --> 01:18:37,710
It's been truly wonderful collaborating closely with the OpenAI technical team to make rapid progress with ROCm.
与 OpenAI 技术团队紧密合作，推动 ROCm 快速进展，这真的非常令人愉快。

882
01:18:37,710 --> 01:18:47,810
To talk about how they are advancing the frontier of software development and our collaboration, I'm delighted to welcome to stage Philippe Tillet from OpenAI.
为了探讨他们如何推进软件开发的前沿以及我们的合作，我非常高兴地邀请 OpenAI 的菲利普·蒂勒登台。

883
01:18:56,040 --> 01:18:57,820
Thank you for joining us here, Philippe.
欢迎你来到这里，菲利普。

884
01:18:58,760 --> 01:19:06,020
So just so you all know, Philippe is the creator of Triton, one of the most important software innovations in modern AI infrastructure.
请大家知道，菲利普是 Triton 的创造者，这是现代人工智能基础设施中最重要的软件创新之一。

885
01:19:06,280 --> 01:19:07,760
It's a huge privilege having you here.
你能来到这里，我们深感荣幸。

886
01:19:08,160 --> 01:19:08,660
Thank you.
谢谢。

887
01:19:12,640 --> 01:19:15,500
OpenAI has always pushed the limits of infrastructure.
OpenAI 一直都在推动基础设施的极限。

